reasoning:
The code directly injects user-controlled path segments (application, profile, label) into repository URIs via String.replace without any canonical base-directory enforcement. In copyFromLocalRepository() it does
    File remote = new UrlResource(StringUtils.cleanPath(getUri())).getFile();
which resolves a file:// URI derived from placeholders. Although StringUtils.cleanPath only normalizes “../” segments, it does not enforce that the resulting file remains under an intended root, nor does it reject absolute or traversal patterns. No check such as target.startsWith(base) or toRealPath(LinkOption.NOFOLLOW_LINKS) is performed. An attacker can supply a path variable containing “..” or an absolute path to traverse outside the intended repository directory, making this a genuine CWE-022 vulnerability.
